{"id": "EUVD-2026-103544", "enisaUuid": "5702d0d8-ef7c-3fd9-aba9-ab7484b81445", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\neth: fbnic: Fix payload page pool error cleanup\n\nThe payload page pool pointer contains an error pointer when its\nallocation fails. The cleanup path passes that error pointer to\npage_pool_destroy() instead of destroying the header page pool. This\ncan dereference the error pointer and leave the header page pool\nallocated.\n\nDestroy the header page pool instead.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4277b19edbc6abc9e1db7d6f6148608e8cb3c34", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4bab07f7b74e59bb26032fa5ff6969d63e1c52ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e0b235bd918d06f54ba8fddd2c3ddc36ca59c15"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98630", "GHSA-4rvg-g69w-74q7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "152bf170-32ef-3261-8739-fb3e1333a237", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a11010fdd9615e8dbb2f5d562ab88caa8a9516a <4bab07f7b74e59bb26032fa5ff6969d63e1c52ef"}, {"id": "19b5da62-321f-39db-a3a8-73a94c109f4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a11010fdd9615e8dbb2f5d562ab88caa8a9516a <8e0b235bd918d06f54ba8fddd2c3ddc36ca59c15"}, {"id": "3050606a-a168-3802-99a0-9ce02fae9868", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "762adaaf-8544-3de6-930c-52b3d9f983aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "7e1246ab-3f18-3a5c-92aa-467cc555e0ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a2a9d6fc-080b-36da-9f8a-f747ba45e406", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d81f0707-889d-3365-ae69-bd